Z||000003||Oreif||11-13-2001||07:18 PM||||The ones that attached to the vent and went up to the roof were called Fi-Air-O scoops. These are no longer available from what I recall. FOCOA has Lazy "C" scoops which attach to the vent and wrap around the sail panel on a notchback Fiero. (Not made for fastback GT) The only other roof scoop is the Indy Scoop which sits in the middle of the decklid and goes over the roof. IRM still makes them. It looks like this:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/All_pics_1.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jncomutt||11-13-2001||09:11 PM||||You can still obtain the Fi-Air-O scoops.  I searched and searched and searched for about a year and a half until I found them.  But what I really found was a $500 price tag.  <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.showcars-bodyparts.com</A>  <P>They're not on the website, they guy is holding out.  After purchasing a few items from him he decided to fax me the Full catalog.  There they were.  Just very very pricy.<P>I suggest you call and talk to the guy if you decide you want them bad enough.  The email support sucks and they might not get back to you.<P>Oh yea, and find out if they have a set already made.  They didn't have the spoiler made when I ordered it (off the web page) and it was taking like 4 months.||||reg||1
